# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent tooling and working documents.
#
# THIS IS A POLICY CHOICE, NOT A DEFAULT. Read it before keeping it.
#
# It suits a repository with one engineer who works on one machine and moves
# work by copying the directory. What a reader of such a repository should see
# is the code and whether it ships, not how one person's development
# environment is wired.
#
# It is the WRONG choice for a team: shared conventions, plans and decision
# records belong in the repo where everyone can review and amend them, and an
# ignored docs/ directory means the only copy lives on somebody's laptop.
#
# Two practical consequences worth knowing before adopting it:
#   - `*.md` ignores README files in subdirectories too. Un-ignore any you
#     actually want tracked, the way !README.md does below.
#   - Anything under the ignored directories is invisible to code review by
#     construction. That is the point, and it is also the risk.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Whole directory, not just settings.local.json: .claude/worktrees/ holds real
# checkouts with their own node_modules, and nothing under it is shared.
.claude/

# Markdown is a personal working artefact here, not a deliverable.
*.md
!README.md
CLAUDE.md

# Keeps agent sessions out of directories that should stay walled off.
.claudeignore

# Agent scratch space
.worktrees/
.superpowers/
